      "id": "sol.amc-8-1986-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The denominator is \\(1 - \\dfrac23 = \\dfrac13,\\) so the expression is \\(\\dfrac{2}{\\frac{1}{3}} = 2 \\times 3 = 6.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E .",
      "hints": [
        "First simplify the denominator \\(1 - \\dfrac23\\)",
        "Dividing by \\(\\dfrac13\\) is the same as multiplying by \\(3\\)"
